      "html": "<p>A licensed e-signature is not a scanned handwriting image. It is a crypto operation that binds the signer to the document at a point in time.</p>\n<h2>Core traits</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Identity:</strong> the certificate is issued after the signer’s data is checked by a licensed authority.</li>\n<li><strong>Integrity:</strong> any edit after signing fails verification.</li>\n<li><strong>Non-repudiation:</strong> the certificate holder cannot easily deny the signature if the private key stayed on the token.</li>\n<li><strong>Device binding:</strong> the private key is not a normal copied file; it is used through the token and software such as ESA.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What that means for invoicing</h2>\n<p>Before an invoice or receipt goes to the tax authority it must be signed or sealed with a valid certificate. ESS creates the document; ESA completes the legal step on the PC.</p>\n<p>Keep the token PIN private and do not use it on an untrusted machine. If the token is lost, tell the signature team during business hours.</p>\n"
